f1 2015 is a jekyll-and-hyde of a video  game in many ways it's the best Formula  One title code masters have ever  released a complete overhaul of the  series driving physics coupled with  wonderfully fun and challenging AI  competitors makes wrestling your car and  the games tracks more fun than ever but  f1 2015 also has an ugly side a shortage  of game modes numerous technical hiccups  and reliability issues that would make  even a Honda mechanic blush make it a  difficult game to recommend there's no  doubt that the on track action is far  better than last year's game but whether  or not you enjoy f1 2015 rest more and  if your favorite mode has been removed  and the frequency by which the game  crushes the desktop okay let's focus on  what works first the driving in this  year's game is the best that's ever been  and it's all down to the handling while  previous games in the series are more  forgiving when it came to traction  control this year's car is more  accurately reflect the high torque  nature of modern f1 this means you can  simply slam on the gas whenever you want  to go fast feathering the accelerator is  a must to ensure you make your way  around the track without spinning this  makes for a far more engaging Drive as  you battle for position and manage your  tyre wear while incoming rain showers  that reduce grip are more terrifying  than in previous games a word of caution  though for those who play with an Xbox  360 pod on their PC the triggers on the  360 controller are much shorter and lack  the Rumble feedback provided on the Xbox  one pad this means that you're required  to use incredible concentration and the  deafness of touches to ensure you don't  power out of a corner and spin your car  the game allows for unlimited flashbacks  and you can always turn traction control  up to full to mitigate these issues but  that kind of removes the most  challenging and enjoyable part of the  game let's just say it may be time to  buy an Xbox one pad for your PC or  better still a wheel and some pedals the  race engineer in f1 2015 is also a lot  more talkative providing a host of  genuinely useful information during  practice sessions through qualifying and  throughout the race itself during your  time in the car he keeps you up to speed  on your strategy on aspects of the track  you should focus your attention on even  notice if you're starting to struggle  with tire wear the engineer is not the  only one that feels more realistic  either the drivers in f1 2015 are well  capable of defending and overtaking  intelligently and of making rash  decisions that force you to take  avoiding action  this makes defending your position as  enjoyable  hunting down the car in front lap after  lap they are capable of making dumb  mistakes but all in all they feel more  human and provide more excitement than  in previous games in this series all  these aspects of driving wrestling the  car toying with race strategy and racing  wheel to wheel against your foes they  kept on 2050 in a game that often  delivers memorable racing moments  though quick race allows you to choose  any track and driver to take part in  everything from a full race weekend in  Melbourne to a short free lap spinner  and Yas Marina the bulk of the games  action takes place in championship  season here you take control of your  favorite f1 driver racing a full career  with practice and qualifying lengths to  your liking f1 2015 also comes with all  the drivers and tracks from last year's  season so you can go back in time from  the options menu if you want to drive  the Hockenheimring or pay your respects  to Jules Bianchi f1 2015 has also added  pro seasons mode which forces you into  full race weekends with realistic race  lengths in this mode you're also forced  to drive from the perspective of the  helmet with no on-screen display against  the toughest of AI competitors so it's  fair to say this isn't for the faint of  heart however the fact that a modified  version of the normal championship mode  receives its own place on the main menu  is telling of just how few ways there  are to play f1 2015 career mode is gone  meaning you can't create your own driver  like in previous games there is also no  co-op of any kind  you can't play locally with a friend in  split-screen anymore or take part in  co-op seasons like in previous games the  multiplayer menu has an option to play  with friends in individual races which  is probably just as well because in days  of trying to connect to any sort of  online Lobby I never once found a game  an entire graphics overhaul means f1  2015 looks better than ever but it's not  without its own issues  disappearing wheels and graphical  glitches take a sheen off an otherwise  great-looking Drive and while the PC at  work allowed me to play a few hours of  barely a hitch my home computer crashed  more than Pastor Maldonado on an opening  lap as wonderfully fun as the racing can  be in f1 2015 few things are more  frustrating than your PC crashing to  desktop after surviving 31 laps around  Marina Bay the game also has no safety  car not even the virtual safety car that  was added to the 2015 season so it's  pretty strange to see a four car pileup  happen behind you in Monaco only for the  race to continue as if nothing happened  and while in game crashes are more  spectacular than ever the car damage is  too inconsistent trauma to the back of  another car and your front wing has as  much chance of being totally unaffected  as it does realistically  breaking into pieces f1 2015 is an  incredibly frustrating game on PC  representing both a wonderful step  forward and a massive stumble serious  technical issues a dearth of game modes  and multiplayer which is functionally  broken on the PC Shara what is otherwise  a wonderful driving game if you can get  f1 2015 to run without crashing on your  machine and you're satisfied playing  championship mode this is a marvelously  fun driving game but just like in  Formula One racing no matter how good  your car feels around the track it cans  for nothing if you can't get it past the  checkered flag reliability is key in  racing right now f1 2015 on PC has far  too little of it  peace  you
 

